title: date_borsalino_3_main
location: day(ship)
---
<<declare $bod3_points = 0>>
<<declare $bod3_investigation_good = 0>>
<<declare $bod3_investigation_bad = 0>>

Today, you are out on the high seas, sailing with Admiral Kizaru!
After the last failed attempt at a date, this should be close to getting *some* time together... Even if it's for a mission.
{$borsalino}: Oh, {$name}! How are *yo~ou...?*
{$borsalino}: We haven't seen each other since... Hmm? The last workday...?
-> Didn't you say you'd take me on a date?!
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
    {$borsalino}: Oh, I did...?
    {$borsalino}: Yes, yes, that rings a bell...
    {$borsalino}: Well, see you later, will—
    {$name}: *Wait.*
    {$borsalino}: ...Okay, okay... I *will* take you out on a date... But for now, we are stuck here together, aren't we...?
-> That was this morning.
    {$borsalino}: Oh, it was?
{$borsalino}: Time is so slow when you're in my shoes...
{$borsalino}: I find it quite comforting to sail like this...
-> Where are we going again?
    <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
    {$borsalino}: Mm... I thought at least one of us was paying attention.
    {$borsalino}: Oh... I'm *ju~ust* kidding... Almost...
-> I suppose it's nice... I always liked to travel.
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
    {$borsalino}: Mmm... I do remember.
-> What sort of mission is this anyway?
    {$borsalino}: Ah... always *so~o* hard-working...
{$borsalino}: We are on our way to the G-9... Something of a diplomatic mission, you see...
{$borsalino}: Inspect the Navy base... Renew treaties... Keep good relations with our allies...
-> Sounds... Very exciting. Yawn.
    {$borsalino} chuckles.
    {$borsalino}: Do you miss the action, {$name}?
    -> Not at all.
        {$borsalino}: O~oh... Good to hear that...
    -> Maybe.
        <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
        {$borsalino}: *O~oh...* Well... Still, you are talented at what you do...
        {$borsalino}: But I'll tell you a secret... I feel the same way sometimes...
        <<jump date_borsalino_3_route1>>
-> I think I'd be good at this.
    {$borsalino}: I'm sure you will... That's why I chose you to come along...
    <<jump date_borsalino_3_route2>>
-> Ew. Not doing business for the World Nobles.
    <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
    {$borsalino} chuckles.
    {$borsalino}: *We~ell...* Don't let them hear you, will you...?
    <<jump date_borsalino_3_route2>>
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route1
location: day(ship)
---

{$borsalino}: ...
He remains in silence for what feels like an hour.
Is he only enjoying the breeze, or is there something else...?
{$borsalino}: You kno~ow—
{$borsalino}: In theory... *Only* in theory... It couldn't hurt to have a look at the crow's nest, could *i~it...?*
{$borsalino}: Only to be sure, ah... That there is no danger...
Borsalino offers you a hand.
-> Yes!
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
    You wrap your fingers around his and...
    **Swoosh!**
    You vanish. The world blurs around you. An incredible force propelling you from under your limbs!
    You appear at the crow's nest and hop down from Borsalino's arms.
    {$borsalino}: You're welcome~...
    Both your coats are wave in the strong, salty wind. Even this massive ship looks tiny from up here. Like on a roller-coaster before the fall, your stomach twists...
    -> Have a look around the surroundings.
        <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
        {$name}: Let me use the rangefinder.
        {$borsalino}: Oh, of course...
        The lens blurs, then focuses in a small shape in the distance.
        Black sails...
        -> Attack!
            <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
            <<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_attack>>
        -> Don't attack.
            <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
            <<jump date_borsalino_3_route_1_notattack>>
    -> Let Borsalino check first.
        <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
        {$borsalino}: Oh... Are you having second thoughts...?
        {$borsalino}: You see, I can just listen in with Haki...
        Despite that, Borsalino looks through the lens.
        {$borsalino}: That seems... Like an enemy ship at a long range from here, dear {$name}...
        -> Attack!
            <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
            <<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_attack>>
        -> Don't attack.
            <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
            <<jump date_borsalino_3_route_1_notattack>>
-> Wait, what are you getting at?
    <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
    {$borsalino}: You'll see, you'll see...
    Huh?! He has disappeared...
    You look around yourself on the empty deck, and squint toward the distance.
    Is that... A pirate ship?
    You're beginning to regret saying anything.
    <<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_call>>
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route1_call
location: day(ship)
---

Your transponder snail rings.
*Berebereberebere...*
-> Ignore the call.
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
    It stopped ringing...
    Borsalino calls the ensign behind you instead.
    {$borsalino}: Ah~ You're avoiding my calls, {$name}?
    {$borsalino}: It's okay... I do that as well...
-> Pick up the call... Pray to any deities that can hear you.
{$borsalino}: Oh... Attention all soldiers, there's enemies on sight...
{$borsalino}: We will be attacking them, *o~okay...?*
{$borsalino}: Refer to {$name} for your orders...
You can just imagine him giving you a wink and a thumbs-up...
<<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_panic>>
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route1_attack
location: day(ship)
---

{$name}: An enemy ship!
{$name}: It's our duty to attack.
Borsalino grins.
{$borsalino}: Of course, of course it is...
{$borsalino}: Listen, {$name}... I think these pirates must be lost, so close to Headquarters...
{$borsalino}: This *wo~on't* be much of a challenge, will it...?
-> I'll go first!
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
    Borsalino chuckles.
    {$borsalino}: I'll be faster, believe me...
-> You go first!
    {$borsalino}: Gladly...
{$borsalino}: The soldiers will listen to you, I bet...
{$borsalino}: Please call all armed men on deck...
{$borsalino}: Have the others ready the artillery...
{$borsalino}: And approach the target as fast as you can...
-> Got it!
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
-> Can you repeat?
    Whoops! He's gone!
You climb your way down as fast as you can. This is going to be fun.
<<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_choose>>
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route1_panic
location: day(ship)
---

Soldiers are gathering on deck, holding their weapons ready. They are looking at you for guidance!
{$name}: Uh...
-> The target is in that direction. Let's try to sail forward.
    Ensign: What did you say?
    Ensign: I can't hear you...
    -> I SAID MOVE!!
        Ensign: O-okay...
        Ensign: Do you mean all five of us on deck, or...?
        What? There are only five people on deck?
        It seems like there are some steps you are missing...
        <<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_secondchance>>
    -> Cry quietly
        Ensign: Oh no... We are doomed...
        <<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_fail>>
-> Call all armed men on deck!
    {$name}: We need to prepare for an incursion!
    You speak into the snail as your subordinates crowd the deck.
    It's not going that bad!
    <<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_success>>
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route1_secondchance
location: day(ship)
---

{$name}: Okay. Let's try this again.
-> Everyone prepare the artillery!
    Ensign: Uh... I'm sorry, {$name}, but we are too far away from the target!
    <<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_fail>>
-> Everyone gather on deck first!
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
    Your unit breaks into formation. coordinate on deck.
    -> Half of you, prepare the artillery!
        <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
        {$name}: The other half should stay on deck and get ready for the incursion.
        {$name}: We sail forward! As fast as we can!
        Determination replaces the confusion that was obvious in your subordinates' eyes. This is not going that bad!
        <<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_success>>
    -> Let's sail toward the enemy as fast as we can!
        <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
        Your men seem confused... This sounded much better in your head.
        <<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_fail>>
-> FIRE!!!
    Ensign 1: Fire?! We haven't even prepared the cannons!!!
    There is a distant explosion, its impact quaking through the sea and tumbling the warship.
    Ensign 2: Oh no, oh no, oh no arewegonnadie?!
    The men hug each other and cry.
    <<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_fail>>
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route1_choose
location: day(ship)
---

You meet a couple of soldiers on deck, holding their weapons ready. They are looking at you for guidance!
Ensign: So... According to the Admiral, you're in charge now! What are your orders, {$name}??
-> Let's attack immediately!
    <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
    Your men look at each other as if they are afraid.
    Ensign: Uh... I'm sorry, {$name}, but what direction is the enemy again?
    {$name}: Ugh...
    You point out what you saw in the crow's nest. Keep a cool head while you think of the next step...
    <<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_secondchance>>
-> Everyone gather on deck first!
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
    Your unit breaks into formation.
    -> Half of you, prepare the artillery!
        <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
        {$name}: The other half should stay on deck and get ready for the incursion.
        {$name}: We sail forward! As fast as we can!
        Determination replaces the confusion that was obvious in your subordinates' eyes. This is not going that bad!
        <<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_success>>
    -> I hope you are all okay that we are stopping the mission to go fight pirates...
        <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
        Your men look at each other as if they don't quite understand. You are unsure, and it's wearing off on them.
        Ensign: Uh... Yes...?
        Ensign: We are ready to heed your orders.
        <<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_secondchance>>
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route1_success
location: day(ship)
---

Your warship propels itself in the enemy ship's direction! You are on deck, the wind tousling your hair, your heart thumping wildly.
Over a megaphone, you shout that the pirates should freeze, because they are surrounded and you're ready to attack!
From the pirate ship's deck, Borsalino waves at you.
{$borsalino}: Why... I already defeated and arrested them all, of course...
{$borsalino}: Care to help me take them to the cells...?
{$name}: Wha- What? Already??
Around you, the rest of the crew seems unfazed.
A few arrests and stacks of paperwork later...
<<set_background office show>>
You return to HQ and the familiarity of the office.
{$borsalino}: Well... The mission got derailed...
-> Let's never do that again?
    {$borsalino}: Aww... {$name}... I thought being spontaneous was what you wanted.
    {$borsalino}: *But...* at least you are honest...
-> That was fun!
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
    {$borsalino}: Hmm... I thought so...
    {$borsalino}: Variety is the spice of life, isn't it?
His hand is quite close to yours... Almost brushing your fingers together.
You put your hand on his. This time he doesn't vanish.
Wow~
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route_1_notattack
location: day(ship)
---

{$name}: Well... They are just minding their own business...
{$name}: I don't think we should derail the mission.
{$borsalino}: Oh, of course... Let's get back on deck, shall *we~e...?*
Borsalino does look a little bit disappointed... or does he? It's hard to tell.
<<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_earlyend>>
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route1_earlyend
location: day(ship)
---

{$borsalino}: Oh... Well, I have some calls to make... Take care...
Borsalino has vanished.
You're about to get to the island and he will be busy the rest of the time...
That didn't go too well!
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route1_fail
location: day(ship)
---

This is going terribly. Call Borsalino for help?
-> Yes.
    You grab the den den mushi...
    {$borsalino}: Hello... Who is this?
    {$borsalino}: {$name}, you are still a little dot in the distance...
    {$name}: Come back... I don't have a grip on this.
    {$borsalino}: Oh... Is that so...?
    <<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_end_bad>>
-> No.
    <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
    You are pretty sure you can manage on your own...
    ...Except someone else already called him for help.
    {$borsalino}: Mmm... Hello~o?
    {$borsalino}: Oh, is it that bad...?
    This is even worse. The worst case scenario!
    <<jump date_borsalino_3_route1_end_bad>>
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route1_end_bad
---
<<set_background day(ship) cross_fade "date_borsalino_3_route1_end_bad_fade">>
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route1_end_bad_fade
---
Back on deck...
{$borsalino}: Well, I had to leave the prisoners unattended...
{$borsalino}: Was that too much for you?
-> I thought we were going on a diplomatic mission!!
    <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
    {$borsalino}: I'm sorry you feel this way...
    {$borsalino}: I think a bit more flexibility wouldn't be bad for you...
    {$borsalino}: ...and that you liked spontaneity...
    {$borsalino}: *Oh!* All is well that ends well, hmm...?
    {$name}: That's what you call well...?
-> Ugh... I overestimated myself...
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
    {$borsalino}: Hmm...
    {$borsalino}: Don't worry about it... This wasn't what we had planned, was it...?
    {$borsalino}: Well... I am quite sure we will have many other opportunities to ah...
    {$borsalino}: Make things more interesting...
    {$name}: Hm...
That certainly could have gone better. Ugh.
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route2
location: day(ship)
---

{$borsalino}: We are almost there... I should call the base...
{$borsalino}: So, see you when we dock...?
-> I have a question about the mission.
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
    How come you are appointed to it?
    {$name}: It seems something a Vice Admiral could do.
    {$borsalino}: Oh, you are so sharp, {$name}.
    {$borsalino}: The truth is... This base is close to the Sorbet Kingdom...
    {$borsalino}: Does that ring a bell...?
    -> I've heard that before.
        <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
        {$name}: They used to be our enemies, didn't they?
        {$borsalino}: *Ve~ery* good...
        {$borsalino}: And that is why the... Ah... *Decisions* we make in this base are important...
        {$borsalino}: They could impact the world, at large...
    -> Not really...
        {$borsalino}: *O~okay,* well...
        {$borsalino}: I'll put it like this... It's important to be on their good side...
-> I will wait here.
    Borsalino nods and smiles at you.
    {$borsalino}: See you soon...
    He disappears in a flash.
-> I'll go below deck.
    <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
    {$borsalino}: Oh, as you please...
    He disappears in a flash of light.
    Uh... It seems like he didn't know that you meant *along* with him...
     Or he wants space...
You try to relax, feeling the salty wind on your face.
The warship creaks around you...
<<set_background day(town) cross_fade>>
You have docked at the base. Much like Marineford, a town has grown around it.
Civilians have gathered at the port to greet the Admiral's ship.
As you step onto the wooden walkway, Borsalino suddenly taps your shoulder.
{$borsalino}: Hello again...
{$borsalino}: I hope I didn't startle you...
-> Ask about the mission.
    {$name}: Did you manage to contact the base?
    {$borsalino}: Oh, I suppose I did?
    {$borsalino}: Truth be told... There was not a lot of talking...
    {$borsalino}: Only barking...
     Borsalino shrugs a shoulder.
-> Look around the port.
    There are generic Marine ships here, but others are antique and luxurious.
    {$borsalino}: Oh... Look at that...
    {$borsalino}: Those ships look like royalty, don't they...?
    {$borsalino}: Very nice...
-> Pout because he keeps disappearing.
    <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
    {$borsalino}: Oh... {$name}...
    {$borsalino}: Business before pleasure, *ye~es...?*
{$borsalino}: What we need to do...
{$borsalino}: Is to find out as much as we can about the **way things work** here... *Oka~ay?*
In the crowd, a big dog with fluffy white hair approaches you. It's wearing a Navy hat.
-> What the hell is that?
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
    Borsalino chuckles.
    {$borsalino}: Oh, so how are we today, Vice Admiral?
    He's addressing the dog...
    {$name}: Um... Are you okay?
    The dog suddenly turns into a tall woman clad in a Navy uniform!
-> Awww! Floofy.
    Borsalino takes a step back towards the dock.
    {$borsalino}: All yours, {$name}...
    You pet the doggo behind the ears.
    {$name}: Who's a good girl? Who's a—
    {$borsalino}: Oh... The dog?
    {$borsalino}: That's a Vice Admiral.
    You immediately stop petting the doggo.
    It turns into a tall woman clad in a Navy uniform... stomping her foot against the dock.
    ?: Woof! Oh, that was nice, I mean... Sorry!
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
    Dog: Vice Admiral Woof at your service!
    {$borsalino}: This is Petty Officer {$name}... They're with me.
    Dog: Pleased to meet you!
    Dog: So, let's get down to business! Where should we start?
    {$borsalino}: The newcomer's *cho~oice...*
    <<jump date_borsalino_3_route2_choices>>
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route2_choices
---
<<if $bod3_investigation_good >= 2 || $bod3_investigation_bad >= 2>>
    {$borsalino}: Ah, actually... I think we have seen enough...
    <<if $bod3_investigation_good >= 2>>
        <<jump date_borsalino_3_route2_good>>
    <<else>>
        <<jump date_borsalino_3_route2_good>>
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    -> Check the Navy offices <<if !visited("date_borsalino_3_route2_office")>>
        <<jump date_borsalino_3_route2_office>>
    -> Check the training grounds <<if !visited("date_borsalino_3_route2_training")>>
        <<jump date_borsalino_3_route2_training>>
    -> Have a look around the town <<if !visited("date_borsalino_3_route2_docks") && !visited("date_borsalino_3_route2_town")>>
        Dog: Yes! A walk! A walk!
        -> Go to the docks
            <<jump date_borsalino_3_route2_docks>>
        -> Go to the housing area
            <<jump date_borsalino_3_route2_town>>
    -> Go to the docks <<if visited("date_borsalino_3_route2_town") && !visited("date_borsalino_3_route2_docks")>>
        <<jump date_borsalino_3_route2_docks>>
    -> Go to the housing area <<if visited("date_borsalino_3_route2_docks") && !visited("date_borsalino_3_route2_town")>>
        <<jump date_borsalino_3_route2_town>>
<<endif>>
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route2_office
location: office
---

You chose to check the offices.
The Navy base is impersonal, as public buildings often are. A known smell of paper and coffee permeates the corridors.
{$borsalino}: Well, well...
{$borsalino}: I'll leave the questions to you, {$name}...
-> Check if their paperwork is up to date!
    Dog: Ha ha ha ha! Up to date? Not here!
    {$borsalino}: O~oh, don't worry, Vice Admiral...
    {$borsalino}: Our situation at HQ is similar.
    It seems like Borsalino was expecting something else...
-> Check that their arrest record is impeccable!
    <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
    <<set $bod3_investigation_bad += 1>>
    Dog: Wow! You've really learned from the Fleet Admiral, huh?
    {$borsalino} chuckles.
    {$borsalino}: {$name} takes the job very seriously...
    It seems like Borsalino was expecting something else...
-> Ask about the structure and chain of command!
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
    <<set $bod3_investigation_good += 1>>
    {$borsalino}: *Oh...?* That's an interesting question...
    Dog: Well, the only real difference between us and most of the bases...
    Dog: Is that we have a department dedicated to cooperating with the guards of the Sorbet Kingdom.
    {$borsalino}: Is that so...?
    -> Tell us more!
        <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
        <<set $bod3_investigation_good += 1>>
        Dog: The tensions between the Government and the Kingdom is very recent!
        Dog: So the monarchy wants to be present in the Navy's operations... This is the solution we found. And it works!
    -> What? You let them control you?
        <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
        <<set $bod3_investigation_bad += 1>>
        Woof tilts her head.
        Dog: It's more like a partnership?
        {$borsalino}: I see... I see...
Dog: Nothing special, huh?
Dog: Where would you like to go next?
<<jump date_borsalino_3_route2_choices>>
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route2_training
location: training grounds
---

You chose the training grounds.
The island seems a lot older here than at the port. The hill this fortress is built on is ancient, with irregular stone peeking out from between the modern concrete.
A unit is going through training drills.
They are a bunch of scrawny girls and boys attempting to throw cannonballs at each other, struggling to even lift them up.
Cadet A: This is the worst...
Cadet B: My manicure!
Cadet C: Pull through... Just... Gasp... One more throw...
Cadet C faints.
{$borsalino}: Hmm... We~ell, what do you think, {$name}?
-> Ridiculous.
    <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
    <<set $bod3_investigation_bad += 1>>
    {$name}: You need to be harder with them, Vice Admiral!
    Dog: Oh...
    Woof pouts, turning her head low.
    {$borsalino}: Hmm... A word, {$name}?
    {$borsalino}: We are trying to be diplomatic with our subordinates, *he~ere...*
-> Well, um...they need a bit of work, don't they?
    Woof nods energetically.
    Dog: We're putting them through the Garp treatment! Heh!
    {$borsalino}: Ooh, I see...
    Borsalino nods, but it seems like he was expecting something else...
-> Where do these cadets come from?
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
    <<set $bod3_investigation_good += 1>>
    Dog: Ah...
    Woof tilts her head.
    Dog: This is our latest unit.
    Dog: They're mostly young nobles? I suppose they send their kids here to straighten them u—
    Dog: OMG BALL!
    Dog: Sorry, sorry...
{$borsalino}: Oh, Vice Admiral... That is all *ve~ery* interesting...
Dog: So! What's the next stop, Name?
<<jump date_borsalino_3_route2_choices>>
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route2_docks
location: day(ship)
---

You chose to go back and have a closer look at those wonderful ships docked here.
Rows and rows of them, their sails wine red and silver, their figureheads shaped like mermaids and fauns.
{$borsalino}: Ooh... Shiny...
-> They look expensive.
    Dog: Royalty ships, woof!
    {$borsalino}: I wonder if we'd have time to sail on one of these after the work is done...
    You blush a little bit.
-> Isn't that a waste of funds?
    <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
    <<set $bod3_investigation_bad += 1>>
    Borsalino chuckles, but the way he looks is cryptic.
    {$borsalino}: We are trying to stay *diplomatic*, dear {$name}...
    Dog: U-uh...actually...some of these are gifts from the World Nobles!
    Dog: Heh. No funds wasted here, right?
-> I'd love to sail on one of these. So fancy.
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
    <<set $bod3_investigation_good += 1>>
    Borsalino smiles and says nothing.
    Dog: Aren't they?!
    Dog: They are m-mostly gifts from the World Nobles...
    Dog: That's how you know they're happy with us!
    {$borsalino}: I see...
Dog: So! What would you like to do next?
<<jump date_borsalino_3_route2_choices>>
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route2_town
location: town
---

You chose to get a feel for the town.
The weather is warm, and the sun is heavy. Some Marines patrol in uniform, but otherwise, the civilians must be with their families.
There's none of the pomp you saw back at the port.
{$borsalino}: Hmm!
{$borsalino}: Reminds me a little of old Marineford...
Borsalino seems distracted, looking at the seafood restaurants. You catch a conversation between two of your colleagues.
Marine A: Hey, {$name}!
Marine A: Things are getting wild out there, with all that's happening...
-> You are right! I'd prefer to be taking down bad guys. I'm so tired of following the Government.(-)
    The two soldiers seem like they agree with you.
    They look proud. They look inspired! They look like... Like they just saw a ghost.
    Oh, he's right behind you, isn't he?
    {$borsalino}: Oh... That was quite an outburst, {$name}...
    -> I'm sorry!
        {$borsalino}: You know... it's good to motivate your subordinates...
        {$borsalino}: But there... Is a time and place, mmm...?
    -> I'm just saying what I think is right!
        <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
        <<set $bod3_investigation_bad += 1>>
        {$borsalino}: Oh, I see...
        {$borsalino}: You could become a very influential person, {$name}.
        {$borsalino}: But pick your battles...
-> I think it depends...
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
    <<set $bod3_investigation_good += 1>>
    {$name}: I agree with you. Action is important.
    {$name}: But we are visiting a country which used to be our enemies too. If we are diplomatic once in a while, we can focus our efforts elsewhere.
    Borsalino catches up with you and whispers into your ear.
    {$borsalino}: Well done, {$name}... They'll listen to you. They like you.
-> Not at all.
    <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
    <<set $bod3_investigation_bad += 1>>
    {$name}: Go back to work!
    {$borsalino}: ...
    Borsalino is signaling at you to follow him.
    {$borsalino}: You can be a little harsh, can't you...? Pick your battles...
Dog: So! Where would you like to go next?
<<jump date_borsalino_3_route2_choices>>
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route2_bad
location: day(ship)
---
{$borsalino}: Ah... Name...
{$borsalino}: Could we have a word...?
{$borsalino}: I can tell you're tired, aren't *yo~ou...?* I will take over from here, if you will...?
Huh? Did you do something wrong?
It's hard to tell what he is thinking.
{$borsalino}: It's *oka~ay...* I still like you...
Borsalino winks at you, but waves you away.
That seemed...to go not so well, you think as you return to the ship.
===

title: date_borsalino_3_route2_good
location: town
---
Dog: Oh! Okay!
Dog: I hope you had a good time! Let's meet up later and do the paperwork.
{$borsalino}: Oh... Sure... Thank you for showing us around, dear Woof.
Woof salutes.
{$borsalino}: Well, well. What do you think?
-> It's a total catastrophe around here.
    <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
    {$borsalino}: Oh, really?
    {$borsalino}: Hmm...
    {$borsalino}: I think this base might just serve its purpose... The, ah, you know... Public relations...? It's all good... The people are happy...
    {$borsalino}: Well... We don't have to agree on everything.
-> I think everything is working as it should.
    <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
    {$borsalino}: I'm glad you see it this way...
-> I think I'm doing your job again!
    <<set $bod3_points -=1>>
    {$borsalino}: Oh. No, no. I want to know what your opinion is... But I do have mine...
    {$borsalino}: It seems a bit... Chaotic... But replacing the Vice Admiral or sending more troops here, ah... It could do more harm than good...
    -> I agree!
        <<set $bod3_points +=1>>
        {$borsalino}: Sometimes inaction is the best action... And not everything is what it seems.
        He smiles. That absent, friendly smile with so much hidden beneath.
    -> I don't see it.
        {$borsalino}: Well... We don't have to agree on everything...
        He smiles. That absent, friendly smile with so much hidden beneath.
{$borsalino}: Let's go have lunch together... hmm?
You smile, feeling like you have made a good impression.
